From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Subject: [PATCH] swupdate-progress: avoid \r in redirected output

When stdout is redirected (e.g. captured by systemd), the progress line
is terminated with \r\n instead of plain \n, causing the carriage return
to appear as a literal character in the journal.  Emit \r only when
writing to a terminal.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/tools/swupdate-progress.c	2026-07-30 10:42:54.168757248 -0400
+++ b/tools/swupdate-progress.c	2026-07-30 10:42:54.167603885 -0400
@@ -404,13 +404,12 @@
 				fill_progress_bar(bar, sizeof(bar), msg.cur_percent);
 
 				if (!silent) {
-					fprintf(stdout, "[ %.*s ] %d of %d %d%% (%s), dwl %d%% of %llu bytes\r",
+					fprintf(stdout, "[ %.*s ] %d of %d %d%% (%s), dwl %d%% of %llu bytes%s",
 						bar_len,
 						bar,
 						msg.cur_step, msg.nsteps, msg.cur_percent,
-						msg.cur_image, msg.dwl_percent, msg.dwl_bytes);
-					if (redirected)
-						fprintf(stdout, "\n");
+						msg.cur_image, msg.dwl_percent, msg.dwl_bytes,
+						redirected ? "\n" : "\r");
 					fflush(stdout);
 				}
 
